      "message": "1 The LMP version in HCI_Read_Local_Version_Information cannot be used to indicate the present of functionalities.\nIn BLUETOOTH CORE SPECIFICATION Version 5.3 | Vol 2, Part C | 2.8 LMP MESSAGE CONSTRAINTS referred that \"The LMP version number is not used to indicate the presence or absence of functionality.\"\n\n2 All of the new features after BT 4.0 are optional\n\n3 The HCI/LMP version should be consistent with the certified version for BQB certification.\n\nSo the HCI/LMP version of the FW would keep being updated following by the BQB certification version; however it will not support any features defined after BT 4.0.",
